@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito66-a-separate-calculation`
IMPORT `ito66-c-credit-points`

-- ===========================================================================
-- s 66(b).  Line 2459.
--
--   (ב) על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (א) ובסעיף 65, בן זוג שהיתה לו הכנסה מרכוש
--       שהיה בבעלותו שנה לפני נישואיו או מרכוש שקיבל בירושה בתקופת נישואיו,
--       רשאי לתבוע שייעשה חישוב נפרד של המס על הכנסתו האמורה, ובלבד שאם
--       היתה לבן הזוג האמור הכנסה אחרת לגביה נערך חישוב מס נפרד, תיווסף
--       ההכנסה על פי סעיף קטן זה להכנסה האחרת.
--
-- "על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (א) ובסעיף 65": the claim stands whether or not a
-- separate calculation is made under (a), and so is not gated by subsection
-- (d), which gates (a) only.  Either spouse may claim ("בן זוג").
--
-- The proviso decides where the income goes once claimed: into the spouse's
-- OTHER separate calculation if there is one, otherwise a calculation of its
-- own.  READING (fork F7): the only "other income for which a separate
-- calculation is made" that s 66 creates is the (a)(1) calculation of the
-- spouse who is not the registered spouse.  The registered spouse's own
-- income is assessed on him under s 65 as modified by (a)(2) and (a)(3), and
-- is not a "separate calculation"; so his (b) income, if claimed, is always
-- calculated on its own.  (Version 0.4.0: F7 is now a switch, below.)
--
-- WHAT IS AN INPUT (version 0.2.0, 02-X2).  The two conditions (b) puts on
-- the property, "שהיה בבעלותו שנה לפני נישואיו" and "שקיבל בירושה בתקופת
-- נישואיו", are not computed: the caller sorts the income into the two (b)
-- fields of `A spouse`, so the one-year edge and the mode and time of
-- acquisition are the caller's to decide (NOTES.md section 1).
--
-- TAX YEARS (version 0.2.0, 02-V4).  The two rules that take the couple, and
-- so carry the tax year, refuse a year before 2024 (A1); the rules on one
-- spouse carry no year and state the deposited text.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 66(b) — income from property owned before the marriage or inherited during it`

@ref s 66(b), line 2459
GIVEN `the spouse` IS A `A spouse`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(b) — the property income of` `the spouse` MEANS
         `the spouse`'s `taxable income from property owned one year before the marriage`
    PLUS `the spouse`'s `taxable income from property inherited during the marriage`

-- "רשאי לתבוע": an entitlement.
@ref s 66(b), line 2459
GIVEN `the spouse` IS A `A spouse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(b) — may claim a separate calculation of the property income:` `the spouse` MEANS
    `s 66(b) — the property income of` `the spouse` GREATER THAN 0

@ref s 66(b), line 2459
GIVEN `the spouse` IS A `A spouse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(b) — the property income is calculated separately:` `the spouse` MEANS
        `s 66(b) — may claim a separate calculation of the property income:` `the spouse`
    AND `the spouse`'s `claims a separate calculation of the tax on the property income in subsection (b)`

-- FORK F7 (version 0.4.0; RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08, SHRUG; inventory
-- 02-F7).  "ובלבד שאם היתה לבן הזוג האמור הכנסה אחרת לגביה נערך חישוב מס
-- נפרד": (i) the only such calculation s 66 creates is the (a)(1) calculation
-- of the spouse who is not the registered spouse, so the registered spouse
-- never has one (the reading of 0.1.0-0.3.0); (ii) once (a)(1) makes a
-- separate calculation, or the registered spouse requests one under (c)(1A),
-- his own calculation is also one, and his (b) income joins it.  The two
-- differ only for the registered spouse, and only where (ii) finds such a
-- calculation; the default declines there.
@ref s 66(b), proviso, line 2459; s 66(a)(1), line 2456; s 66(c)(1A), line 2462; fork F7; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of the proviso to section 66(b) as to the registered spouse`
`section 66(b) — the reading this row takes of the proviso as to the registered spouse` MEANS
    `declined where the readings of the proviso to section 66(b) differ`

@ref s 66(b), proviso, line 2459; fork F7
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the proviso to section 66(b) does not say whether the registered spouse's own calculation is other income for which a separate calculation is made` MEANS
    REFUSE "the proviso to section 66(b) does not say whether the registered spouse's own calculation is other income for which a separate calculation is made"

GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A `A reading of the proviso to section 66(b) as to the registered spouse`
`the reading of the proviso to section 66(b) taken for` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER couple's `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `section 66(b) — the reading this row takes of the proviso as to the registered spouse`
    WHEN JUST rs THEN rs's `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse`

@ref s 66(b), proviso, line 2459; s 66(a)(1), line 2456; s 66 amendment list, line 2454; fork F7
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      which  IS A `Which spouse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(b) — for` couple `, the spouse has other income for which a separate calculation is made:` which MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (CONSIDER which
         WHEN `registered spouse` THEN
             CONSIDER `the reading of the proviso to section 66(b) taken for` couple
             WHEN `only the separate calculation under (a)(1) is other income for which a separate calculation is made`
                 THEN FALSE
             WHEN `the registered spouse's own calculation counts once (a)(1) or (c)(1A) makes a separate calculation`
                 THEN `under (ii)`
             WHEN `declined where the readings of the proviso to section 66(b) differ`
                 THEN IF   `under (ii)`
                      THEN `the proviso to section 66(b) does not say whether the registered spouse's own calculation is other income for which a separate calculation is made`
                      ELSE FALSE
         WHEN `spouse who is not the registered spouse` THEN `s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` couple)
    WHERE
        `under (ii)` MEANS
                `s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` couple
            OR  `s 66(c)(1A) — a separate calculation of income from personal exertion is requested by the` `registered spouse` `in` couple

DECLARE `Where the property income in subsection (b) goes` IS ONE OF
    -- no claim: it is income not from personal exertion like any other
    `it is not calculated separately`
    -- the proviso
    `it is added to the spouse's other income for which a separate calculation is made`
    -- the main clause
    `it is calculated separately on its own`

@ref s 66(b), line 2459; s 66 amendment list, line 2454
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      which  IS A `Which spouse`
GIVETH A `Where the property income in subsection (b) goes`
`s 66(b) — for` couple `, the property income goes:` which MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (BRANCH
            IF   NOT `s 66(b) — the property income is calculated separately:` (`the particulars of the` which `in` couple)
            THEN `it is not calculated separately`
            IF   `s 66(b) — for` couple `, the spouse has other income for which a separate calculation is made:` which
            THEN `it is added to the spouse's other income for which a separate calculation is made`
            OTHERWISE `it is calculated separately on its own`)
